hadiths[82]{hadithnumber,text}:
"63001","Yahya related to me that Malik had seen that the people of knowledge used to like to pay the zakat al-fitr after dawn had broken on the day of the Fitr before they went to the place of prayer. Malik said"
"63002","Yahya related to me that Malik had seen that the people of knowledge used to like to pay the zakat al-fitr after dawn had broken on the day of the Fitr before they went to the place of prayer. Malik said"
"63101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"63102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"63201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"63202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"63301","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that once in the time of Uthman ibn Affan the new moon had been seen in the afternoon and Uthman did not break his fast until evening had come and the sun had set. Yahya said that he had heard Malik say that some one who sees the new moon of Ramadan when he is on his own should start the fast and not break it if he knows that that day is part of Ramadan. He added"
"63302","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that once in the time of Uthman ibn Affan the new moon had been seen in the afternoon and Uthman did not break his fast until evening had come and the sun had set. Yahya said that he had heard Malik say that some one who sees the new moon of Ramadan when he is on his own should start the fast and not break it if he knows that that day is part of Ramadan. He added"
"63401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"63402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"63501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his
father that he said to Umar ibn al-Khattab, ""There is a blind she-
camel behind the house,'' soUmar said, ""Hand it over to a household so
that they can make (some) use of it."" He said, ""But she is blind.""
Umar replied, ""Then put it in a line with other camels."" He said, ""How
will it be able to eat from the ground?"" Umar asked, ""Is it from the
livestock of the jizya or the zakat?"" and Aslam replied, ""From the
livestock of the jizya."" Umar said, ""By AIIah, you wish to eat it.""
Aslam said, ""It has the brand of the jizya on it."" So Umar ordered it
to be slaughtered. He had nine platters, and on each of the platters
he put some of every fruit and delicacy that there was and then sent
them to the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him
peace, and the one he sent to his daughter Hafsa was the last of them
all, and if there was any deficiency in any of them it was in Hafsa's
portion.


""He put meat from the slaughtered animal on the
platters and sent them to the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless
him and grant him peace, and he ordered what was left of the meat of
the slaughtered animal to be prepared. Then he invited the Muhajirun
and the Ansar to eat it.""


Malik said, ""I do not think that
livestock should be taken from people who pay the jizya except as
jizya."""
"63502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that A'isha and Hafsa"
"63601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as Saidi that the Messenger of Allah"
"63602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as Saidi that the Messenger of Allah"
"63701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Harmala al- Aslami from Said ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"63702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Harmala al- Aslami from Said ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"63801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman that Umar ibn al-Khattab and Uthman ibn Affan would pray maghrib when they saw the night darkening"
"63802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman that Umar ibn al-Khattab and Uthman ibn Affan would pray maghrib when they saw the night darkening"
"63901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari from Abu Yunus"
"63902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari from Abu Yunus"
"64001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd Rabbih ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from A'isha and Umm Salama"
"64002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd Rabbih ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from A'isha and Umm Salama"
"64101","I was related to by Malik, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab rode a horse in the cause of Allah, and he wanted to buy it back. He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: \Do not buy it back"
"64102","Ziyad related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that some men among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were shown Laylat al-Qadr in a dream, in the last seven nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I see that your dreams have agreed concerning the last seven nights. So"
"64201","Ziyad related to me from Malik, that he heard from someone he trusted among the people of knowledge."
"64202","Yahya related to me from Malik, from someone he trusted among the people of knowledge, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shown the lifespans of the people before him, or what Allah willed of that. It was as if he found the lifespans of his Ummah to be short, so that they would not achieve what others had achieved with long lives. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, gave him Laylat al-Qadr, which is better than a thousand months."
"64301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that a certain man kissed his wife while he was fasting in Ramadan. This made him very anxious"
"64302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that a certain man kissed his wife while he was fasting in Ramadan. This made him very anxious"
"64401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"64402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"64501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Atika bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl"
"64502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Atika bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl"
"64601","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', that Abdullah ibn Umar used to only give dates for Zakat al-Fitr, except for one occasion when he gave barley."
"64602","Yahya related to me from Malik, that he asked Ibn Shihab about a man who is in I'tikaf, can he go under a roof for his needs? He said: Yes, there is no harm in that."
"64701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Abu Hurayra and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas used to say that someone who was fasting was allowed to kiss"
"64702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Abu Hurayra and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas used to say that someone who was fasting was allowed to kiss"
"64801","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that A'isha"
"64802","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that A'isha"
"64901","Yahya said that Malik said that Hisham ibn Urwa ibn az-Zubayr had said"
"64902","Yahya said that Malik said that Hisham ibn Urwa ibn az-Zubayr had said"
"65001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about people kissing while fasting and he said that he allowed it for old men but disapproved of it for young men"
"65002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about people kissing while fasting and he said that he allowed it for old men but disapproved of it for young men"
"651","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to forbid kissing and fondling for people who were fasting"
"652","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"653","Yahya related to me from Malik, that it reached him that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to his governor in Damascus concerning Sadaqah: Sadaqah is only in crops, gold and silver, and livestock."
"654","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"655","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami once said to the Messenger of Allah"
"656","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used not to fast while travelling"
"657","Yahya related to me from Malik that Hisham ibn Urwa said"
"658","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"659","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Hunayd ibn Abd arRahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayra that a man broke the fast in Ramadan and the Messenger of Allah"
"660","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ata ibn Abdullah al-Khurasani that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"661","Malik said, ""I have heard people of knowledge saying that the kaffara specified by the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, for a man who has intercourse with his wife during the day in Ramadan is not due from someone who, on a day when he is making up the fast of Ramadan, breaks his fast by having intercourse with his wife, or whatever. He only has to make up for that day."" Malik said, ""This is what I like most out of what I have heard about the matter."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to be cupped while he was fasting. Nafi said, ""He later stopped doing that, and would not be cupped when he was fasting until he had broken the fast"
"662","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and Abdullah ibn Umar used to be cupped while they were fasting"
"663","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to be cupped while he was fasting and he would not then break his fast. Hisham added"
"664","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"665","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan say from the mimbar on the day of Ashura in the year in which he made the hajj"
"666","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab had sent (the following message) to al-Harith ibn Hisham"
"667","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from alAraj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"668","Yahya related to me from Malik that he used to hear the people of knowledge say"
"669","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"670","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"671","[671] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Samman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah that he used to say : Whoever has money and does not pay his zakat, on the Day of Resurrection, he will be represented as a brave man, bald, having two raisins that he seeks. He could even say: I am your treasure, a foothold in front of Malik Hadith: 671 Arabic Hadith:"
"672","[672] Yahya told me on the authority of Malik: He read the book of Omar ibn al-Khattab about charity. He said, “And I found in it: In the name of God.” The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. The Book of Sadaqah: In twenty-four camels, followed by sheep, in every fifth there is a sheep, and in what is above that up to five. And thirty Ibn Makhad, and if it is not Ibn Makhad, then Ibn Labun is a male, and beyond that, up to forty-five daughters. Labun, and beyond that up to sixty, the number of stallions’ trouks, and beyond that up to seventy-five jad’ahs, and among On top of that, up to ninety pints of Labun, and on top of that, up to two hundred and twenty hqqatas of the stallion’s strands, and whatever exceeds that. That is one of the camels, so in every forty there is a Bint Labun, and in every fifty there is a camel, and in the cattle of the sheep, when they reach forty to One hundred and twenty sheep, and beyond that up to two hundred sheep, and beyond that up to three hundred, three A sheep, and whatever is more than that, for every hundred sheep, and no he-goat, or an old woman, or one with a defect, shall be given in charity, except Whatever the believer wishes, and he does not combine what is divided, and he does not separate between people for fear of truthfulness, and he is not of two mixtures. So they will retract each other according to what is equal, and when the ruqyah is equal to five uwaqs, a quarter of a tenth is equal to Imam Malik Hadith: 672 Arabic Hadith:"
"673","Yahya related to me, from Malik, from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki, from Tawus al-Yamani, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal al-Ansari took thirty cows that were one year old and forty cows that were two years old. He was brought what was less than that, and he refused to take anything from it, saying, \I have not heard anything about it from the Messenger of Allah"
"674","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his brother Khalid ibn Aslam that Umar ibn al-Khattab once broke thefast on a cloudy day thinking that evening had come and the sun had set. Then a man came to him and said"
"675","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"676","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibr Shihab that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra differed about making up days missed in Ramadan. One of them said that they were done separately and the other said that they were done consecutively. He did not know which one of them it was who said that they were done separately"
"677","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"678","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab being asked about making up days missed in Ramadan"
"679","Yahya related to me from Malik that Humayd ibn Oays al-Makki told him"
"680","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that A'isha and Hafsa"
"681","Yahya related to me, from Malik, from one he trusted, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, and from Busr ibn Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: For what is watered by the sky, springs, and natural irrigation, it is one-tenth (al-'ushr), and for what is watered by irrigation (al-nadh), it is half of one-tenth (nisf al-'ushr)."
"682","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked about what a pregnant woman should do if the fast became difficult for her and she feared for her child"
"683","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father used to say"
"68401","[684] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, On the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: A Muslim does not have to pay any zakat in his slave, nor in his horse.\\nMutta Imam Malik hadith: 684 Arabic Hadith:"
"68402","[684] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, On the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: A Muslim does not have to pay any zakat in his slave, nor in his horse.\\nMutta Imam Malik hadith: 684 Arabic Hadith:"
"685","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman that he heard A'isha"
"686","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge telling people not to fast on the day in Shaban when there was doubt (about whether it was Shaban or Ramadan)"
"687","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"688","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"689","Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik from his father that Abu Hurayra said"
